1|# Verification: forge Homegrown web backend (Muse P2 + Claude loop fix), pre-deploy — 2026-11-02
2|Target: ~/projects/forge @ 2faf9d9 (deploy/modal_web.py, app/backend/{budget,config,image_files,limits,loop,selfcheck,stream}.py, app/web/{index.html, app.js}, app/tests/*)
3|Evidence: reports/forge-web-backend-2026-11-02.evidence/
4|Verdict: FAIL
5|
6|> [!summary] **NO-GO for deploy until 4 fixes land: 1 that breaks the page, 3 that let money go out uncounted.** S1-S7 are mostly implemented well.
7|> - **W1 (blocker, sent early):** `api.mount("/", StaticFiles…)` comes **before** the API routes, so it swallows them. Tested with fastapi 0.115.6 in the same order: `GET /api/status` → 404, `POST /api/build` → 405. No test covers the ASGI app, which is why 69 tests pass.
8|> - **W2:** `/api/status` calls `GET {FORGE_URL}/v1/models` on every request, with no rate limit. Hypothesis from the Modal docs, not run: a request to a scaled-to-zero function boots the A100. A cold probe is usually followed by a charged warm-up ($0.45). But the probe also boots when the warm-up throttle says no, and polling more often than every 300 s **keeps the GPU warm with nothing charged**, since warm probes cost nothing on the counter.
9|> - **W3:** spend is only charged on a `done` event with code. Timeouts, model errors, crashes without code and **closed browser tabs** are never charged.
10|> - **W4:** after the 600 s timeout, `rates.release()` frees the slot, but the worker thread keeps calling the model (up to 3 × 600 s). The concurrency limit and the spend count both slip.
11|>
12|> The real hard ceiling today is modal_forge's `max_containers=1`: ≈ $2.50/h ≈ $60/day plus sandboxes, whatever the $20 counter says.
13|
14|## Scope
15|Asked by the coordinator (Claude for Alyssa, m…18, free): review Muse P2 + the Claude loop fix before any deploy. It covers:
16|- S1-S7;
17|- path traversal in /files;
18|- secrets;
19|- anything that could spend money without limit.
20|
21|Deploy waits for the user's yes (cap $20; high/xhigh open). Read-only; reviewed at 2faf9d9. Since then forge HEAD moved (1c2af7b … 45ea141). 1c2af7b moves the static mount last: I checked the order only (mount at line 378, after the 4 routes at 224-354), with no TestClient run. The W2-W4 fixes are prompted for Muse P2b (978c611), not yet built. I ran pytest in a `git archive` copy, and a FastAPI mount-order probe in a scratch venv (/tmp/verifier-forge-web; fastapi 0.115.6 + httpx from PyPI). No Modal or model calls. Target state is in evidence/00.
22|
23|Requirements:
24|- R1: S1 self-check;
25|- R2: S2 image;
26|- R3: S3 limits;
27|- R4: S4 cost cap;
28|- R5: S5 time;
29|- R6: S7 privacy;
30|- R7: the loop = FTX;
31|- R8: the routes work;
32|- R9: no uncounted spend;
33|- R10: secrets and /files safety.
34|
35|## Code
36|- [WRONG] (R8) **the static mount swallows the API** — source: deploy/modal_web.py (inside `web()`: `api.mount("/", StaticFiles(directory=…/app/web, html=True))` precedes `@api.get("/api/status")`, `@api.post("/api/build")`, `@api.post("/api/lead")`, `@api.get("/files/{filename}")`); evidence/01-mount-order.txt (the same order, TestClient: `GET / 200`, `GET /api/status 404`, `POST /api/build 405`)
37|  - Fix W1: mount the static files **after** all routes;
38|  - add a TestClient test of `/api/status`, `/api/build` (SSE), `/api/lead` and `/files` with fakes. FastAPI isn't in .venv, so add it as a test dependency.
39|- [WRONG] (R9) **status wakes the GPU, uncharged** — source: deploy/modal_web.py `probe_model()` and `status()`; app/backend/budget.py (`status`, `may_warmup`, `note_warmup`); Modal docs via context7 ("Functions autoscale … automatically boots a container in response to an initial input"; min_containers 0 → scales from zero); deploy/modal_forge.py (scaledown 300 s)
40|  - every `/api/status` (unauthenticated, no rate limit) sends a request to modal_forge. Hypothesis (Modal docs; not run): if it's cold, that request starts the A100. From the cold starts measured in earlier sessions (200-601 s; reports/forge-exam-pre-2026-11-02 evidence/02, forge-product-spec), a boot plus the 5 min idle ≈ $0.35-0.63;
41|  - a cold probe followed by a fired warm-up is charged $0.45, about one boot. But a boot from the probe while the throttle refuses the warm-up, and all keep-alive from polling inside the 300 s scale-down, are **not** charged. A crawler polling every few minutes keeps the GPU up at ≈ $60/day while the counter barely moves;
42|  - Fix W2: don't call FORGE_URL to learn whether it's warm. Use `modal.Function.from_name("forge-trained", "serve").get_current_stats()` (container counts, no input) or an in-process "warm until" time from the last real call. Probe only when it's known warm. Charge WAKE_USD whenever **any** request (status, warm-up or build) reaches a cold model.
43|- [WRONG] (R9) **uncharged build paths** — source: deploy/modal_web.py `build()` → `_aiter` (`money.charge_build` only inside `if ev["step"] == "done" and ev.get("code")`), `_bounded` (TimeoutError branch, `finally: rates.release()`); app/backend/loop.py (`run_job` yields done with gpu_seconds only at the end)
44|  - not charged:
45|    - (a) the 600 s timeout;
46|    - (b) an exception from `next(gen)`;
47|    - (c) a done without code (model error, no code fence);
48|    - (d) the visitor closing the tab (the StreamingResponse generator is cancelled);
49|  - also: a model call that fails in a later round never adds its seconds (`gpu_total` counts only successful calls);
50|  - Fix W3: accumulate model seconds in `_model_call` (successful or not) into a per-build counter, and charge it plus the sandbox fee in `_bounded`'s `finally`, on every exit path. Keep the idle-tail rule.
51|- [PARTLY] (R3, R9) **a slot is released while work continues** — source: deploy/modal_web.py `_bounded` (`asyncio.timeout(BUILD_LIMIT_S)` + `finally: rates.release()`); `_aiter` (`asyncio.to_thread(next, gen, _END)`); `_model_call` (`post_chat(body, timeout=600)`)
52|  - cancelling the async side doesn't stop the thread. A timed-out or abandoned build keeps calling the model (up to 3 × 600 s) and the box, while its slot is already free, so more than `MAX_CONCURRENT_BUILDS` generations can run;
53|  - Fix W4: pass a deadline into the loop (each `post_chat` timeout = the remaining build time; stop between rounds once past it), and release the slot only when the worker thread has ended.
54|- [VERIFIED] (R1) S1: `self_check` returns PASS only for a built part with 1 solid **and** a parsed overall size matching the sorted extents within 0.5%. BUILT ("size not checked") when no size parses; CHECK FAILED otherwise. Overall size is parsed **only** by OVERALL, BOXNOUN or BASE_WALL (a bare "base …" without the wall-height phrase isn't a size). The docstring says "when unsure, return BUILT, never PASS" — source: app/backend/selfcheck.py
55|  - note: the comparison is order-free (sorted), so an axis swap passes. That's documented, and the badge line says what was checked.
56|- [VERIFIED] (R7) the loop = FTX rules, including the Claude fix — source: app/backend/loop.py; experiments/first-test/runner.py:206-208,577-599; runner_final.py do_bx_cloud_call
57|  - `initial_messages = runner_final.ft_messages`; the body is `runner.build_body(…, reasoning_strength=config.reasoning_strength())`, which equals `runner.build_bx_body` at the default "xhigh";
58|  - a crash → `bx_error_message`; a build → `bx_self_check_message` and another call; a reply with no code fence ends it; ≤ 3 calls; the last built part counts.
59|- [VERIFIED] (R2) S2: the image gets only the explicit `WEB_IMAGE_FILES` (app/web, app/backend, runner_final.py, cloud_cq.py, run_cq_box.py, runner.py, checks.py, budget_left.py). `check_file_list` rejects expected.json, jobs.py, jobs.jsonl, results/ and data/, and `cloud_cq` is imported inside `web()` only for `run_answer_in_box` — source: app/backend/image_files.py; deploy/modal_web.py `_web_image()`
60|  - note: `app/web/dev_server.py` is in the image and served at `/dev_server.py`. Harmless, but drop it from WEB_FILES.
61|- [VERIFIED] (R3, R10) S3 and safety — source: deploy/modal_web.py; app/backend/limits.py; app/tests (no-secret greps)
62|  - `max_containers=1` + an asyncio lock;
63|  - `client_ip` takes the **last** X-Forwarded-For hop, else the peer (hypothesis: Modal's proxy appends exactly one hop);
64|  - run ids are `uuid4().hex`;
65|  - `/files/{filename}`: a path param (no `/`), the extension whitelisted (stl/step/py), used only as a Modal Dict key, so **no filesystem path and no traversal**;
66|  - the VLLM key comes only from the Modal secret.
67|
68|## Experiments & examples
69|- [VERIFIED] (R1-R7) `pytest -q app/tests` → 69 passed in a clean archive of 2faf9d9. But no test imports FastAPI or calls the ASGI app (test_p2_web.py is 7 CSS/static checks), so W1-W4 can't show up — source: evidence/02-pytest.txt; app/tests/test_p2_web.py
70|- [VERIFIED] (R5) S5: BUILD_LIMIT_S 600; WEB_TIMEOUT_S 720 > the limit; the first event (`write`) is yielded before the first model call; `with_heartbeat` sends `: heartbeat` every 15 s from a pump task — source: app/backend/config.py; app/backend/stream.py; loop.py `run_job`
71|
72|## Data
73|- [PARTLY] (R4) S4 cost model as coded: GPU seconds = model-call latency × $0.000694 + $0.002 + an idle tail of $0.21 once per burst (gap > 300 s) + WAKE $0.45 per fired warm-up; throttle 1 per 10 min globally and 1 per hour per IP; spend mirrored to a Modal Dict by UTC day. The rules are right, but W2 and W3 bypass them, and DAILY_CAP_USD = 20 still needs the user's yes — source: app/backend/budget.py; app/backend/config.py
74|  - the honest ceiling today: modal_forge `max_containers=1` ≈ $2.50/h ≈ $60/day plus sandboxes and the web CPU;
75|  - suggest a Modal billing alert at the user's number as a second guard (hypothesis: available in the workspace settings).
76|- [PARTLY] (R6) S7 — source: app/web/index.html:141; deploy/modal_web.py `lead()`. The form shows "We only use your email to reply about Homegrown. To delete it, email us or send the form again with 'delete' as the tool."
77|  - no address is given;
78|  - `/api/lead` has no delete handling (a 'delete' simply appends another record) and no rate limit (the whole list is rewritten each time).
79|
80|  Fix: name a contact address; delete by hand; add a per-IP limit on /api/lead.
81|- [VERIFIED] (R10) the page escapes model output: app.js has one `innerHTML` (the marquee track copying itself); code and details are set as text — source: app/web/app.js:28 (grep)
82|  - note: the three.js import map loads from jsdelivr without SRI (import maps can't carry integrity in all browsers). Pin the exact version, as now, or self-host.
83|
84|## Rubric
85|Rubric: completeness 5/10 · clarity 6/10 · depth 8/10 → needs work (FAIL until W1-W4)
86|
87|Requirements R1-R10: fully met are R1, R2, R5, R7 and R10, so 5/10 → 5. Partly met: R3 (the slot), R4 (the rules bypassed), R6 (privacy). Not met: R8 (routes) and R9 (uncounted spend).
88|
89|Clarity (items listed): 11 of 18 items are resolved:
90|1. the PASS/BUILT/FAILED rules;
91|2. the parse patterns;
92|3. the file list;
93|4. the forbidden names;
94|5. max_containers + lock;
95|6. last-hop IP;
96|7. uuid ids;
97|8. /files safety;
98|9. 600/720/heartbeat;
99|10. the loop = FTX;
100|11. secrets.
101|
102|7 are open: the route order, the status probe, uncharged paths, slot release, the lead limit and delete, the contact address, dev_server served. 11/18 → 6.
103|
104|Depth: what goes wrong is given for 15 of 18 (all but the uuid, heartbeat and secrets items). 15/18 → 8.
105|
106|| Item | What | Status | Source | If unresolved |
107||---|---|---|---|---|
108|| W1 | mount StaticFiles **after** the API routes; add FastAPI TestClient tests for all 4 endpoints | **must-fix (blocker)** | evidence/01 | the live demo never reaches the API |
109|| W2 | status must not send a request to a cold model (use get_current_stats or an in-process warm-until); charge WAKE on any cold boot | **must-fix (money)** | modal_web.py probe_model/status; Modal docs | unthrottled, uncounted A100 boots (up to ≈ $60/day) |
110|| W3 | charge model seconds + the sandbox fee on every exit path (timeout, error, no code, disconnect) | **must-fix (money)** | modal_web.py _aiter/_bounded | spend escapes the $20 counter |
111|| W4 | a deadline inside the loop (per-call timeout = time left); release the slot when the thread ends | **must-fix (money/limits)** | modal_web.py _bounded/_model_call | more than 2 generations; work after timeout |
112|| N1 | /api/lead: a per-IP limit; a contact address for deletion; drop dev_server.py from the image | must-do (small) | index.html:141; image_files.py | spam; a privacy promise with no path |
113|| N2 | a Modal billing alert at the user's cap; keep FORGE_URL private (anyone with it can boot the A100, even with 401s) | note | modal_forge max_containers=1 | — |
114|
115|## Verdict
116|**FAIL: NO-GO for deploy** (at 2faf9d9; W1's order fix 1c2af7b looks right, but it needs a TestClient test) until W1 (routes) and W2-W4 (uncounted spend, slot release) are fixed and covered by TestClient tests. S1, S2, S3 (apart from the slot), S5 and the FTX loop are verified. The user's yes on DAILY_CAP_USD (and high/xhigh) is still needed after that.

